    "body": "WidgetStore uses hashes for widget artwork filenames and stored-path lookups. I found that `hash` acquired `SHA-1`, while the MessageDigestSpec rule accepts `SHA-256`, `SHA-384`, `SHA-512`, `SHA256`, `SHA384`, and `SHA512`.\n\nI changed the current artwork hash entry point to SHA-256 and added a shared resolver that moves existing SHA-1-named artwork to its SHA-256 destination. Stored snapshot paths now resolve through that migration path during decoding, and pruning retains both recorded paths and migrated destinations. The legacy SHA-1 derivation remains limited to locating existing artwork, with migration guarded by a shared lock.\n\nThe digest is part of the name of a file the app stores (WidgetStore.kt, line 161), so the change renames existing files to the new name before they are opened instead of leaving them behind.\n\nI found this while running the app under RVSec, a runtime checker for how apps use the Java crypto and TLS APIs.\n\nThe project builds with this change (`:app:assembleCoreDebug`).\n\nI'm a Computer Engineering student at the University of Brasília (UnB), working on a research project on Android app analysis. Happy to adjust this to the project's conventions.",
